    "commissioning.flow_title": "How Commissioning fits together",
    "commissioning.flow_intro": "Prove that what was built actually works before anyone signs for it: register the systems, check each one against a pre-functional and then a functional list, raise an issue wherever a check fails, and watch readiness climb until the system can be handed over.",
    "commissioning.flow_1_title": "Register systems",
    "commissioning.flow_1_desc": "List every system to be commissioned with its type and location, so nothing turns up unclaimed at handover.",
    "commissioning.flow_2_title": "Run the checks",
    "commissioning.flow_2_desc": "Work the pre-functional list first, then the functional tests, recording each check as passed, failed or not applicable.",
    "commissioning.flow_3_title": "Raise issues",
    "commissioning.flow_3_desc": "A failed check becomes an issue with a severity and an owner, so it is closed out and retested rather than forgotten.",
    "commissioning.flow_4_title": "Reach readiness",
    "commissioning.flow_4_desc": "Readiness is the share of applicable checks passed. A system at 100 percent with no open critical issue is ready to commission.",
    "commissioning.flow_connects": "Connects with:",
