    "deadlines.flow_title": "How the Deadline register fits together",
    "deadlines.flow_intro": "One list of everything on the project that has a date attached and has not been answered yet. It does not create deadlines of its own; it gathers the dates other modules already hold so nothing quietly runs out of time.",
    "deadlines.flow_1_title": "Dates are set upstream",
    "deadlines.flow_1_desc": "A response date on a letter, a due date on an NCR corrective action, a due date on a punch item. Each is set in its own module.",
    "deadlines.flow_2_title": "The register gathers them",
    "deadlines.flow_2_desc": "Everything still outstanding with a date is pulled together here, grouped by the module it came from.",
    "deadlines.flow_3_title": "Standing and severity",
    "deadlines.flow_3_desc": "Each item is marked overdue, approaching or on time, and carries a severity so the critical ones stand out.",
    "deadlines.flow_4_title": "Act in the source",
    "deadlines.flow_4_desc": "Open the item to answer it where it lives. Once it is answered or the date is met it drops off this list.",
