    "quantities.subtitle": "Collect project quantities, from AI text input, PDF drawings, or CAD/BIM models",
    "quantities.converter_title": "How CAD/BIM Conversion Works",
    "quantities.converter_desc": "Upload your CAD/BIM files (.rvt, .ifc, .dwg, .dgn) and the DDC converter extracts all elements into a structured table, walls, slabs, columns, doors, windows, with calculated volumes, areas, and quantities. AI then maps these elements to cost items and generates a complete BOQ automatically.",
    "quantities.download_converters": "Download DDC Converters",
    "quantities.converter_path": "Install to: ~/.openestimator/converters/",
    "quantities.title": "Quantity Takeoff",
  "quantities.intro_title": "Pick the right way to measure",
  "quantities.intro_body": "Choose how to collect quantities, from a written description via AI, from PDF drawings, or from CAD and BIM models, and install the converter modules the file formats need. Each route turns drawings or models into measured quantities that flow into your BOQ.",
  "quantities.intro_more": "This page is a chooser, not a measuring tool itself. It helps you pick how to collect quantities and makes sure the file converters you need are installed. Three method cards send you to the right place: a written description goes to **Quick Estimate (AI)**, PDF drawings go to **PDF Takeoff**, and CAD or BIM models go to the **Data Explorer**. A \"How it works\" strip lays out the upload, measure and apply steps.\n\nThe converter section is the practical part:\n\n1. See which CAD and BIM converters (DWG, RVT, IFC, DGN) are installed.\n2. Install the one your file format needs, with a one-time download and a progress panel.\n3. Update or uninstall a converter when a newer build is available.\n\n**Getting the most out of it:** Install the converter that matches your incoming files before you start a takeoff, so the model route works the first time. Whichever method you pick, the measured quantities end up in your **BOQ**. For a few numbers you do not need any of this, jump straight to the BOQ editor with Quick Manual Entry.",
