    "field_time.working_time.hours_derived": "Worked out from the start, the end and the break.",
    "field_time.working_time.intro": "Some countries oblige an employer to record when each worker started and stopped on each day, to write it down within days rather than weeks, and to keep it for years. Choose the regime that applies to this site and the record is kept as the hours are booked. Choose none and nothing here asks anything of you.",
    "field_time.working_time.summary_milog": "An employer must record the start, the end and the duration of each worker's daily working time within seven days of the work, and keep that record for at least two years. A main contractor is liable for its subcontractors' minimum wage, which is why the employer is named on every line.",
    "field_time.working_time.empty_hint": "The record is built from the hours already booked here. Book a day, give its lines a start and an end, and it appears in this list.",
    "field_time.working_time.no_regime_hint": "No recording regime is set on these days, so nothing is said about when each record was due or how long it has to be kept. The times themselves are still listed.",
    "field_time.working_time.line_hint": "Give each labour line a start and an end and its hours come from them, less the break. A worker booked to two cost codes needs two segments that do not overlap, not the same hours twice.",
    "field_time.working_time.excluded_one": "{{count}} corrected timesheet is left out so the same hours are not counted twice.",
