    "certified_payroll.how.title": "How certified payroll works",
    "certified_payroll.how.intro": "On public works a contractor has to submit a payroll every week showing who worked, what trade they worked as, the hours they worked each day, and the rate they were paid, with a signed statement that the rate meets the wage determination covering the job.",
    "certified_payroll.how.step1": "Record the wage determination the awarding body issued, and add each craft to it with its basic hourly wage and its fringe benefit rate kept apart.",
    "certified_payroll.how.step2": "Classify each worker under the craft they work in, and state how much of their pay is basic wage and how much is fringe.",
    "certified_payroll.how.step3": "Open a week. Its rows are built from the payroll hours already recorded, so nothing is typed twice.",
    "certified_payroll.how.step4": "Fix whatever the compliance checks report, then sign the statement of compliance. Signing freezes the week, and a correction is issued as a new payroll for the same week.",
    "certified_payroll.how.related": "Works with:",
    "certified_payroll.how.no_rate_table": "No wage rates ship with this product. Determinations are set per craft, per county and per awarding body, and are reissued on their own schedule, so what you record here is the document you were given. The system keeps track of which determination was used and what it said, never a copy of somebody else's schedule.",
