    // ── Computed t() keys: English from the producing vocabulary ──
    // Every key below is assembled at runtime from a token that arrives out of
    // the database or a backend enum, so the key name is a value and not a
    // literal anyone can grep for. These families had no members here at all,
    // which meant the screen showed the token itself, lightly disguised: the
    // default replaced the underscores and stopped there, so a reader saw
    // "on hold" where the product means "On hold". Each wording below comes
    // from the vocabulary's producer, the enum or check constraint or seeded
    // list that decides what the token can be, not from the call site that
    // happens to render it.
    // scripts/check_i18n_computed_keys.py holds the families still unlabelled,
    // so a new computed key cannot appear here without being accounted for.
